<section class="about" id="about" data-section="2">
    <div class="wave-divider wave--dark-to-light"></div>
    <div class="about__inner">
        <h2 class="about__title">The body speaks a language<br>older than words</h2>
        <p class="about__text">Rhythmic Transmitters is an AHRC-funded creative technology project exploring how human expressive movement can be observed, translated, and transmitted through digital media.</p>
        <blockquote class="about__quote">
            <p>What happens when the invisible gesture becomes data —<br>and the data becomes art again?</p>
        </blockquote>
        <p class="about__text">Working at the intersection of performance, kinematic observation, and real-time visual processing, we develop new ways to make the inner qualities of human movement visible. Performers move to live piano and voice while their gestures flow through TouchDesigner and MediaPipe into living chromomorphic forms — colour, light, and shape that breathe with the performer.</p>
        <p class="about__text">Each planet in the chromomorphic cosmos carries a phenomenal colour quality — Saturn's contemplative indigo, Jupiter's expansive orange, Mars' courageous red, the Sun's radiant gold. These formative colour-qualities become the field through which gesture is translated into digital light.</p>
        <p class="about__text">The project sits within Birmingham City University's CreaTech Frontiers programme, bringing together artists, technologists, and researchers to explore what happens when ancient movement practices meet contemporary digital tools.</p>
    </div>
</section>
